@e11jah , just a kind reminder:

The `max-index-length' in MySQL(with InnoDB) is [hard-coded to 3072](https://dev.mysql.com/doc/refman/8.0/en/innodb-limits.html#:~:text=The%20index%20key%20prefix%20length,REDUNDANT%20or%20COMPACT%20row%20format.), but it is configurable in TiDB because of some histroical reason:

https://docs.pingcap.com/tidb/dev/tidb-configuration-file#max-index-length

